# ==============================================================================
# PROJECT JANUS MINI (16-TILE): YOSYS LOGIC SYNTHESIS SCRIPT
# ==============================================================================
# Synthesizes the integrated Tier 4 Digital Top (janus_tier4_top) into a generic
# gate-level netlist.
#
# NOTE ON ASIC MEMORY ARCHITECTURE & 850+ KBIT ROM STORAGE:
# Project Janus RTL incorporates ~851,968 bits (~104 KiB) of precomputed lookups:
#   - CRT Adder Tree: 16 channels x 256 entries x 136 bits = 557,056 bits (~68 KiB)
#   - Compute RNS Encoder: 16 channels x 8 bytes x 256 entries x 8 bits = 262,144 bits (~32 KiB)
#   - JIR Redundant Encoders: 2 channels x 8 bytes x 256 entries x 8 bits = 32,768 bits (~4 KiB)
#
# In a physical ASIC tapeout, these arrays are instantiated as dense compiled
# diffusion ROM hard macros (area: ~0.08 um^2/bit @ 7nm) rather than synthesizing
# millions of discrete NAND2 gates.
#
# Usage (with Yosys installed):
#     yosys synth.ys
# ==============================================================================

# 1. Read Verilog Sources
read_verilog -sv rns_encoder.v
read_verilog -sv crt_adder_tree.v
read_verilog -sv jir_fault_monitor.v
read_verilog -sv janus_tier4_top.v

# 2. Check Integrated Design Hierarchy
hierarchy -check -top janus_tier4_top

# 3. High-Level Synthesis & Elaboration
proc; opt; fsm; opt; memory; opt

# 4. Flatten Arithmetic Multipliers & Modular Adders
techmap; opt

# 5. Clean & Print Area Statistics
clean
stat -top janus_tier4_top

# 6. Write Gate-Level Netlist
write_verilog -noattr janus_tier4_synth_netlist.v
